   "summary": "“China has neither the right nor the moral basis to dictate to the Philippines how and with whom we cooperate to defend our sovereignty and national interests,” DND spokesperson Assistant Secretary Arsenio Andolong said in a statement. READ: DND: PH does not need Beijing’s permission on defense ties “We do not need Beijing’s permission regarding our relations with other nations, especially on matters of our defense and security,” he added.",
   "summary_zh": "“中国既无权，也缺乏道德依据来 dictates 菲律宾应如何以及与谁合作，以捍卫我们的主权和国家利益。”国防部发言人、助理部长Arsenio Andolong在一份声明中表示。阅读：DND：菲律宾无需北京批准即可开展防务关系“我们不需要北京就我们与其他国家的关系，尤其是防务与安全事务，作出批准。”他补充道。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "“China has neither the right nor the moral basis to dictate to the Philippines how and with whom we cooperate to defend our sovereignty and national interests,” DND spokesperson Assistant Secretary Arsenio Andolong said in a statement. READ: DND: PH does not need Beijing’s permission on defense ties “We do not need Beijing’s permission regarding our relations with other nations, especially on matters of our defense and security,” he added. Andolong said China is fueling the very tensions it blamed on other countries. “China’s deceptive accusations against other countries of escalating tensions have gone too far, while it continues to use coercion, intimidation and force to assert its illegal claims in the West Philippine Sea and other waters,” he said. The DND issued its statement a day after Senior Col. Chen Xi, spokesperson for China’s Ministry of National Defense, accused certain Filipino politicians of drawing outside powers into the South China Sea dispute when asked about the Philippine-Australian defense pact. Chen claimed that such efforts would only heighten tensions and undermine regional stability. “Relevant nonregional countries should earnestly respect China’s sovereignty and rights and interests in the South China Sea, and stop meddling in the South China Sea issue,” Chen said in remarks shared by the Chinese Embassy in Manila on Thursday. In its statement, the Armed Forces of the Philippines said its efforts to strengthen territorial defense and maritime security were aimed at protecting the country and upholding the rules-based international order. “As a sovereign nation, the Philippines is free to pursue defense and security cooperation with like-minded countries,” the AFP said. Your subscription could not be saved. Please try again. Your subscription has been successful. For comprehensive coverage, in-depth analysis, visit our special page for West Philippine Sea updates . Stay informed with articles, videos, and expert opinions",
