   "title": "Kano govt dismisses Kwankwaso’s EFCC allegations against Governor Yusuf",
   "url": "https://www.premiumtimesng.com/news/top-news/928415-kano-govt-dismisses-kwankwasos-efcc-allegations-against-governor-yusuf.html",
   "domain": "premiumtimesng.com",
   "source": "Premium Times（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:45:51 +0000",
   "_dt": 1795790751.0,
   "ageDays": 0.82,
   "summary": "The Kano State Government dismissed allegations by former Governor Rabiu Kwankwaso that Governor Abba Yusuf instigated the Economic and Financial Crimes Commission ( EFCC ) to investigate him. In a statement by the Commissioner for Information and Internal Affairs, Sunusi Bature, the state government said Governor Yusuf was not involved in Mr Kwankwaso’s case with the anti-graft agency.",
   "summary_zh": "卡诺州政府驳斥了前州长拉比乌·克旺克瓦索的指控，称州长阿巴·优素福曾指使经济和金融犯罪委员会（EFCC）调查他。州信息与内政事务专员苏努西·巴图雷发表声明说，在克旺克瓦索先生与该反腐机构有关的案件中，优素福州长并未参与。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Kano State Government dismissed allegations by former Governor Rabiu Kwankwaso that Governor Abba Yusuf instigated the Economic and Financial Crimes Commission ( EFCC ) to investigate him. In a statement by the Commissioner for Information and Internal Affairs, Sunusi Bature, the state government said Governor Yusuf was not involved in Mr Kwankwaso’s case with the anti-graft agency. “The government wishes to state categorically that Governor Abba Kabir Yusuf has absolutely no involvement in Kwankwaso’s dealings with the EFCC. Senator Kwankwaso has had engagements with the anti-corruption agency long before the emergence of the present administration in Kano State. “It is therefore wrong, misleading and politically motivated for him to associate Governor Yusuf with an issue that predates the current government,” the statement said. Earlier on Friday, Mr Kwankwaso—who is running as the 2027 vice-presidential candidate of the Nigeria Democratic Congress (NDC)—accused his former political protégé of abusing their 43-year relationship by weaponising state institutions against him and his political allies. Responding to claims of interference in opposition affairs, the state government also distanced Governor Yusuf from ongoing court cases involving the NDC. It stated that the legal proceedings stemmed from internal disagreements within the party and have nothing to do with the state administration. “It is becoming increasingly clear that Senator Kwankwaso is attempting to use Governor Yusuf as a convenient target to attract public sympathy and political relevance ahead of the 2027 general elections,” the statement read. The administration urged the former governor to focus on resolving the internal challenges within his political camp rather than blaming the state government for his political difficulties. “The government also rejects Kwankwaso’s attempt to link Governor Yusuf with the internal crisis and court cases involving the NDC. These are internal party matters arising from disagreements within the NDC, and the Kano State Government has no involvement whatsoever in the legal proceedings. Reiterating that Governor Yusuf was elected to deliver governance rather than engage in endless political disputes, the statement warned that voters in Kano are well-aware of current political developments. “You cannot win public sympathy through blackmail and unfounded allegations,” the government stated, adding that those relying on such tactics should prepare for the verdict of the electorate at the polls in 2027. The statement added that Governor Yusuf remains focused on development and the welfare of the people of Kano State",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
