   "title": "PM expresses gratitude to CSAT supervisors, promises to look for ways to lessen burden next year",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/education/20261126/pm-expresses-gratitude-to-csat-supervisors-promises-to-look-for-ways-to-lessen-burden-next-year",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:37:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1795689422.0,
   "ageDays": 1.99,
   "summary": "Prime Minister Han Seong-sook expressed gratitude Thursday to test supervisors at last week's annual college entrance exam, saying they must have remained on edge throughout the test due to a series of measures added to prevent cheating and that the government will look for ways to minimize their burden next year.",
   "summary_zh": "首相韩成淑周四向上周年度大学入学考试监考人员表示感谢。她说，为防止作弊而采取的一系列措施使监考人员在整个考试期间想必始终绷紧了神经，政府将在明年寻找减轻其负担的办法。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Prime Minister Han Seong-sook expressed gratitude Thursday to test supervisors at last week's annual college entrance exam, saying they must have remained on edge throughout the test due to a series of measures added to prevent cheating and that the government will look for ways to minimize their burden next year. Thousands of additional personnel, usually school teachers, were mobilized to supervise the College Scholastic Ability Test (CSAT), known as Suneung in Korean, to enforce a series of anti-cheating measures, including checking test-takers' glasses and clothing. \"This year's Suneung was an unfamiliar experience for both students and teachers,\" Han said on X. \"As teachers checked the students' glasses and clothing, they likely remained on edge until the very end, anxious about whether anything had been overlooked, yet equally concerned that an unnecessary suspicion might hurt a student's feelings.\" \"When you receive notice of your supervisor assignments next year, we want you to feel more at ease than you did this year, and to that end, we will explore ways to minimize the responsibilities placed on supervisors,\" she said",
