   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The U.S. government on Wednesday (November 25, 2026) announced a tariff of 25% on goods imported from India in response to India’s “unreasonable acts, policies, and practices” that “burden or restrict U.S. commerce”. This is the second-highest tariff among the 14 economies against which the latest action has been taken, second only to the 35% tariff levied on Vietnam.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。美国政府周三（2026年11月25日）宣布，对从印度进口的商品征收25%的关税，以回应印度那些“加重或限制美国商业”的“不合理行为、政策和做法”。在此次最新措施所针对的14个经济体中，25%的关税位居第二，仅次于对越南征收的35%关税。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The U.S. government on Wednesday (November 25, 2026) announced a tariff of 25% on goods imported from India in response to India’s “unreasonable acts, policies, and practices” that “burden or restrict U.S. commerce”. This is the second-highest tariff among the 14 economies against which the latest action has been taken, second only to the 35% tariff levied on Vietnam. The Supreme Court on Wednesday (November 25, 2026) orally observed that students who have already opted for three languages for the current academic year may continue with that option , and need not compulsorily switch back to two languages. Actor Prakash Raj will join the Cockroach Janata Party’s ‘Save Democracy, Save Constitution’ rally in Nagpur on Thursday (November 26, 2026). CJP founder Abhijeet Dipke announced this at a press conference in Nagpur on Wednesday (November 25). He was accompanied by CJP‘s co-convenor Ashutosh Ranka and Ajinkya Shinde. “This public meeting is important because the democratic institutions in this country are being stifled. Vote theft has started happening in every State,” Abhijeet Dipke said, adding that the Gokul election showed how the BJP did not want to lose even a local milk federation election. The Centre of Indian Trade Unions (CITU) has announced a march of one lakh workers to Parliament on December 1 to demand a universal pension of ₹21,000, a minimum wage of ₹42,000 and a tax on super-rich families, among other things. Economist Jayati Ghosh, who addressed a press conference in New Delhi on Wednesday (November 25, 2026) along with CITU leaders, supported the proposed march and said the country is at the point of an “inequality emergency,” and the workers’ march will be a historic occasion. Days after the killing of the last local Lashkar-e-Taiba (LeT) recruit in Kashmir, the Jammu and Kashmir Police on Wednesday (November 25, 2026) shifted their focus to locals operating from Pakistan-occupied Kashmir (PoK) and attached the properties belonging to seven such individuals. After its decisive victory in the last week’s Panchayati Raj elections, the Opposition Congress in Rajasthan on Wednesday (November 25, 2026) took control of 24 of the 37 zila parishads which elected their heads, while the ruling Bharatiya Janata Party secured 10 Zila Pramukh posts despite having a majority in just five rural district bodies. A crash involving a fuel tanker ignited a massive fire on a major highway surrounding Cairo on Wednesday (November 25, 2026), killing at least 30 people, Egyptian authorities said. Andy Taylor, the original guitarist of the 1980s English new wave band Duran Duran , whose huge pop hits include “Hungry Like the Wolf,” “The Reflex” and “Rio” and whose rise up the charts was inextricably linked to the launch of MTV, has died. He was 65. It was London in Geneva on Wednesday (November 25, 2026), a day after Berlin in Geneva. If the first game of the World Chess Championship featuring the Berlin Defence opening ended in a draw by a repetition of moves on Tuesday (November 24), it was a similar story in the second game : the London System battle was also drawn by repetition. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
